// The **language-level** built-in type names — `Iterator`/`Future`/`Sender`/`Receiver`, produced by
// `iter()`/`async`/`.await`/`channel()` — are still reserved (E0049): their values are backend
// builtins dispatched by name, so a same-name user type would be silently shadowed. Registered
// extern types (`Uuid`, `Response`, …) are NOT reserved any more — they are namespace-scoped and
// `use`-imported, so a user may freely declare one (see `structs/user_type_shadows_native.noe`).
// expect: error E0049 at 7:8
struct Iterator { x: int }
